    <briefdescription>
<para>This structure contains ML-KEM encapsulation/decapsulation parameters. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Both operations share the same layout and are mutually exclusive, so a single generic parameter set is used:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>For encapsulation, KeyAddr/KeyLen refer to the input public (encapsulation) key and CtAddr is the output ciphertext.</para></listitem><listitem><para>For decapsulation, KeyAddr/KeyLen refer to the input secret (decapsulation) key and CtAddr is the input ciphertext. The key is supplied either directly through KeyAddr/KeyLen or from the ASU key vault through KeyId. Exactly one of the two must be non-zero, as enforced by XAsu_KmValidateKeyAddrNdKeyId. </para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>    </detaileddescription>
    <location file="/proj/xhdsswstaff1/bhawanas/patch_integration/auto_jobs/esw_github_doxy/git/2026.2/embeddedsw/lib/sw_services/xilasu/src/common/xasu_mlkeminfo.h" line="104" column="1" bodyfile="/proj/xhdsswstaff1/bhawanas/patch_integration/auto_jobs/esw_github_doxy/git/2026.2/embeddedsw/lib/sw_services/xilasu/src/common/xasu_mlkeminfo.h" bodystart="104" bodyend="116"/>
